<!--
    S8 "goto-quality" sub-stage: excise a SUPPLIED single-entry region and emit a
    call to a synthesized pseudofunction in its place.
    Option `outline off|<fn>:<head>-<exit>[;...]` (default OFF, ELEM 4124).

    Stage 2 of inline identification.  Stage 1 (`almostregion`,
    tests/stages/kuna-almostregion.xml) FINDS candidate inlined regions; this
    ACTS on one.  The region is supplied as the option value rather than taken
    from stage 1, so a human reading the code - or an LLM agent reading stage
    1's report - drives the transform directly.  The function entry is part of
    the grammar because an option value is global to the run.

    THE WITNESS (self-contained, no relocations, no calls).

        entry:  eax = edi ; if (esi == 0) goto JOIN
        BODY:   eax += 7                          <- head  0x40100a
                if (eax <= 50) goto BODY2
                eax -= 3
        BODY2:  eax *= 3
        JOIN:   eax += 100 ; ret                  <- exit  0x401018

    BODY is a three-block single-entry region with one edge entering it (the
    entry block's fall-through) and one value live out (EAX).  Outlining it
    replaces the whole body with one call whose argument and result are that
    same EAX.

    WHAT THE LIVENESS HAS TO GET RIGHT, all three of which are in this witness:
      - direction.  The entry block's own `test esi,esi` writes the flags that
        its `je` reads.  Counting any outside read as a live-out flags that and
        rejects the region, so liveness is computed over the region's
        CONTINUATION (blocks reachable from the exit).
      - sub-register aliasing.  The x86 32-bit writes zero-extend, so SLEIGH
        writes both EAX and RAX at the same offset; unmerged, one register
        counts as two live-outs and v1 declines.
      - branch operands.  A CBRANCH carries its destination as a varnode in the
        code space.  It is an address, not a value, and counting it makes the
        `jle` look like a memory read.

    PASS 1 (`option outline off`, the default) = the inlined body, verbatim.
    PASS 2 (the region supplied) = one call, and the body is gone.

    Asserts are counted across BOTH passes, so a token that appears once per
    pass asserts min=max=2 and a token unique to one pass asserts min=max=1.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000">
f30f1efa89f885f6740e83c00783f8327e0383e8036bc00383c064c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401000" name="ol"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option warnstyle banner</com>
  <com>option outline off</com>
  <com>lo fu ol</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option outline 0x401000:0x40100a-0x401018</com>
  <com>lo fu ol</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="outline #1: OFF is the bug - the inlined body is spliced into the caller (pass 1 only)" min="1" max="1">v1 = a0 \+ 7;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="outline #2: OFF - the body's own branch is present too (pass 1 only)" min="1" max="1">if \(0x33 &lt;= v1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="outline #3: ON - the whole region becomes one call named after the region head (pass 2 only)" min="1" max="1">a0 = outlined_0x40100a\(a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="outline #4: ON - the report names the block count and the recovered signature (pass 2 only)" min="1" max="1">outline: excised 3 block\(s\) at 0x40100a into outlined_0x40100a\(\) \(1 argument\(s\), 1 result\(s\)\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="outline #5: ON - the excised body is gone, so its multiply appears in pass 1 only" min="1" max="1">v1 \* 3;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="outline #6: the surrounding function is untouched in both passes (off plus on = 2)" min="2" max="2">return a0 \+ 100;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="outline #7: the guard that reaches the region is untouched in both passes (off plus on = 2)" min="2" max="2">if \(a1\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
